---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Reference"
  description="The UniDPP reference material: the framework in full, the standards map, the implementation, comparisons, trust, papers, terminology, and stewardship."
  eyebrow="04 · Reference"
>
  <h1>Reference</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The reference material, stated in full. Pages are factual: standards citations,
    repository contents, capability tables, and stewardship records. Corrections by pull
    request are welcome.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="contents-heading">
    <h2 id="contents-heading">Contents</h2>
    <dl class="index-list">
      <div>
        <dt><a href="/reference/framework/">Framework</a></dt>
        <dd>The fourteen invariants in full, the six-layer architecture, the lens model, profile axes, capability classes, the twin axis, and the resilience doctrine.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><a href="/reference/standards/">Standards</a></dt>
        <dd>The topics map with steward bodies, the EU profile as one jurisdiction among others, the twelve seams, and the profile landscape.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><a href="/reference/implementation/">Implementation</a></dt>
        <dd>The open reference implementation: repositories, languages, modules, and the conformance corpus.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><a href="/reference/compare/">Comparisons</a></dt>
        <dd>A factual capability comparison of freeDPP, OpenDPP, and UniDPP, sourced from the public repositories of each project.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><a href="/reference/trust/">Trust</a></dt>
        <dd>The SIGNATIF-shaped trust model: registry, co-signatures, revocation readings, and stamps.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><a href="/reference/papers/">Papers</a></dt>
        <dd>The catalogue of planned contributions to ISO/IEC JTC 5 and partner bodies.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><a href="/reference/terminology/">Terminology</a></dt>
        <dd>The multilingual Glossarist edition of the Digital Product Passport vocabulary.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><a href="/reference/about/">About</a></dt>
        <dd>Stewardship across the partner bodies, governance, licensing, and contact.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .index-list {
    margin: 1.4rem 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    max-width: var(--prose);
  }
  .index-list div {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: 0.85rem 0;
  }
  .index-list dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }
  .index-list dt a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .index-list dt a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .index-list dd {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
